Z||000008||johnt671||12-12-2001||11:07 AM||||I got some nice heat shielding from Jeg's.  It's just like the plastic loom but made out of a aluminum foil material with a lining in it.  Don't recall the gauge  of the cable but I know I asked for the longest cable they made, and it was to long.  Auto parts store should be able to look up the gauge, but I'd get the next size up due to  the extra length.  Also get some wire ties and keep it away from anything metal or the Fiero gremlin will push it against it. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pheagey||12-13-2001||12:17 AM||||   Alright!, Got that all sorted out now.<BR>Headed to Discount and got my '+' terminal wore then to a local pro shop and got some heat sheilding tubing. The cable BARLY! fit thru it but it made it all the way. total cost: 15.76, getting to my interview on time(and getting the job): priceless.<BR>   Man I need to get another car, something I can beat the h*ll out of, like a civic...<BR>   Anyways, I did get it done and alls well. Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed, custome paint job<BR>"I! have a plan!"<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>Killed: '97 civic CS auto;<BR>Killed by: '94 Civic Ex, '96 Camery LX<BR>Vandalised: 2 time (in 2 days).||||reg||1
